{
  "name": "CE-02 | Video Clips (Omni -> Veo -> Manual)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CE-02 | Video Clips\n**Trigger:** every 5 minutes. Each run makes **one scene clip** (clips are ~8 s each), so a 4-scene Short takes about 4 runs.\n\n**Flow**\n1. Reads the **Content** tab and picks one row with `status = Approved` (new) or `Rendering` (in progress) that is not locked.\n   *Daily cap:* a NEW video only starts if fewer than `maxVideosPerDay` were started today.\n2. Locks the row for 20 min (`lock_until`) so overlapping runs can't double-generate (and double-bill) a clip.\n3. Looks in `workDir/<id>/` to see which `scene_N.mp4` files already exist and takes the first missing scene.\n4. **Provider chain** (column `video_provider`, default `omni_api`):\n   - **Omni Flash** API -> downloads the clip file.\n   - if Omni fails at any step -> **Veo 3.1** (submit, wait/poll every 30 s, download).\n   - if Veo fails too (or `video_provider = manual_drop`) -> **Manual**: you get an email with the exact prompts and file names; status becomes `Awaiting Manual Clips` and CE-03 takes over.\n5. Saves the clip, releases the lock, logs which provider made it in `provider_used`.\n6. When all scenes exist -> status `Clips Ready` (CE-04 assembles the video).\n\n**Cost safety:** clips already on disk are never regenerated. Omni costs roughly $0.10 per second of 720p video (check Google's pricing page).\n\n**Edit in Config node:** sheetId, workDir, omniModel, veoModel, maxVideosPerDay, notifyEmail, manualFolderId.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 600,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "083d441e-1869-53fd-abe0-752737c161a9",
      "name": "Note - How this works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        -120
      ]
    },
